    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 3 USER]\ne019\tWillow Hub can give us a room and promote the sessions.\ne020\tI had been talking as if they would also coordinate locally, but their director clarified that they cannot promise staff time.\ne021\tOur volunteer lead still wants to do it.\ne022\tShe says new volunteers are more likely to join something that feels like growth than something described as fixing operations.\ne023\tI partly agree, and I partly think we are using inspiration to avoid the unglamorous work.\n[Turn 3 ASSISTANT]\ne024\tThe room and promotion are meaningful, but local coordination was carrying more of your imagined model than you realized.\ne025\tVolunteer excitement can be a source of capacity, yet it is risky to count people before they have committed to specific shifts and responsibilities.\ne026\tYou could test that assumption directly: recruit for named roles at the second site before announcing a launch.\ne027\tIf the energy is real, it should translate into some concrete ownership, though not necessarily all the ownership you need.",
