    "prior_context": {
      "alternative_citation_allowed": true,
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 2 USER]\ne011\tYou are treating the current variation as a warning sign, but some of it is normal.\ne012\tParticipants work shifts, care for relatives, and come when they can.\ne013\tThe people who attend repeatedly have learned a lot—we have stories of people applying for jobs and managing appointments online.\ne014\tI do not want “stable attendance” to become a standard that excludes the reality of the people we serve.\n[Turn 2 ASSISTANT]\ne015\tThat is an important correction.\ne016\tConsistency in this setting may need to describe the program's availability and learning quality, not the same people attending every week.\ne017\tThe question could be whether participants can enter irregularly and still receive coherent help, and whether volunteers can deliver that without improvising everything.\ne018\tExpansion might serve the mission even with variable attendance, provided the operating model is designed for variability rather than judged against a classroom ideal.",
